{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLRCKaUWEeGwAKpZeom2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Lb9FVhdM3v7tGH148nVf2","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","query":"global"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1409,"cache_read_input_tokens":31108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1409},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5d16116-a17f-46b7-8be6-774b4bf3878f","uuid":"66e2c9c8-ac83-438a-b951-d9876f0b1556","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:18:29.394Z","request_id":"req_011CgLRCKEPSMiy1rXL9LHrp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019Lb9FVhdM3v7tGH148nVf2":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","query":"global"}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019Lb9FVhdM3v7tGH148nVf2","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Lb9FVhdM3v7tGH148nVf2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"c57716bd1b210b880f9ad7b096569454b3783048","date":"2026-09-21T18:21:18+03:00","message":"(chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app (#372)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app\n\nAdd swr to the reports app's peerDependencies so the build tooling\nfederates it, and pin the exact 2.5.1 dependency the way the other\npackages in this repo do so the fallback copy matches the app shell.\n\nThe openmrs rspack config derives the module federation shared list\nfrom peerDependencies. swr was only reaching the reports app\ntransitively, so the built entry registered no swr share and bundled a\nprivate copy. useSWR from that copy reads its own SWRConfig context,\nnot the one the framework's component decorator provides, so the\nreports app ran with SWR's stock defaults (revalidate on focus and\nreconnect, unlimited retries on every error) and its own cache instead\nof the shared one. The other four packages here already declare the\npeer.\n\nWith the peer declared, the built entry registers swr, swr/_internal,\nswr/immutable and swr/infinite at 2.5.1, matching the other O3 apps.\n\n* Invalidate report lists through the SWR config's mutate\n\nThe cancel modal refreshed the report tables with the global mutate\nimported from swr. That function is bound to SWR's default cache, while\nevery hook rendered under the framework's component decorator lives in\nthe decorator's provider cache, so once swr is federated the global\nmutate no longer reaches those hooks and the tables would not refresh\nafter a cancel or delete. Take mutate from useSWRConfig instead, which\nis bound to the provider cache, and wrap the helper in useCallback so\nthe submit handler's dependency list stays honest.\n\n---------","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"398480586cac283f44ee70737f174da84ae78f23","date":"2026-08-21T15:56:46+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5848: Render visit summary config read-only without Manage Global Properties (#316)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Amrita P.","authorEmail":"153388147+BlessedAmrita@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7798df7ddeed23cb02e4150345588967b95de09b","date":"2026-06-05T15:37:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Pin swr to 2.2.5 to match the app shell and avoid share-scope skew (#290)","refs":"","body":"swr is shared as a Module Federation singleton across the O3 frontend.\nesm-system-admin-app and esm-admin-openconceptlab-app declared it as a\ncaret range, which floated up to 2.3.3, while the app shell\n(@openmrs/esm-app-shell) and most apps pin swr exactly to 2.2.5. Two swr\nminor versions then register into the shared scope, and singleton\nresolution binds consumers by container init order. When swr/immutable\nand swr/infinite at 2.3.3 bind against the shell's eager swr/_internal\nat 2.2.5, SWRGlobalState.get(cache) returns undefined and the patient\nchart crashes on render (TypeError: undefined is not iterable),\nintermittently failing distro e2e runs.\n\nPinning swr to 2.2.5 in both packages aligns them with the app shell.\nPart of a coordinated set of pins (canonical PR:\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app#757).","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":3}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5d16116-a17f-46b7-8be6-774b4bf3878f","uuid":"a9f0c6ef-3f67-4f4d-9987-95ca3f22fa02","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:18:29.465Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"c57716bd1b210b880f9ad7b096569454b3783048","date":"2026-09-21T18:21:18+03:00","message":"(chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app (#372)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app\n\nAdd swr to the reports app's peerDependencies so the build tooling\nfederates it, and pin the exact 2.5.1 dependency the way the other\npackages in this repo do so the fallback copy matches the app shell.\n\nThe openmrs rspack config derives the module federation shared list\nfrom peerDependencies. swr was only reaching the reports app\ntransitively, so the built entry registered no swr share and bundled a\nprivate copy. useSWR from that copy reads its own SWRConfig context,\nnot the one the framework's component decorator provides, so the\nreports app ran with SWR's stock defaults (revalidate on focus and\nreconnect, unlimited retries on every error) and its own cache instead\nof the shared one. The other four packages here already declare the\npeer.\n\nWith the peer declared, the built entry registers swr, swr/_internal,\nswr/immutable and swr/infinite at 2.5.1, matching the other O3 apps.\n\n* Invalidate report lists through the SWR config's mutate\n\nThe cancel modal refreshed the report tables with the global mutate\nimported from swr. That function is bound to SWR's default cache, while\nevery hook rendered under the framework's component decorator lives in\nthe decorator's provider cache, so once swr is federated the global\nmutate no longer reaches those hooks and the tables would not refresh\nafter a cancel or delete. Take mutate from useSWRConfig instead, which\nis bound to the provider cache, and wrap the helper in useCallback so\nthe submit handler's dependency list stays honest.\n\n---------","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"398480586cac283f44ee70737f174da84ae78f23","date":"2026-08-21T15:56:46+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5848: Render visit summary config read-only without Manage Global Properties (#316)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Amrita P.","authorEmail":"153388147+BlessedAmrita@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7798df7ddeed23cb02e4150345588967b95de09b","date":"2026-06-05T15:37:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Pin swr to 2.2.5 to match the app shell and avoid share-scope skew (#290)","refs":"","body":"swr is shared as a Module Federation singleton across the O3 frontend.\nesm-system-admin-app and esm-admin-openconceptlab-app declared it as a\ncaret range, which floated up to 2.3.3, while the app shell\n(@openmrs/esm-app-shell) and most apps pin swr exactly to 2.2.5. Two swr\nminor versions then register into the shared scope, and singleton\nresolution binds consumers by container init order. When swr/immutable\nand swr/infinite at 2.3.3 bind against the shell's eager swr/_internal\nat 2.2.5, SWRGlobalState.get(cache) returns undefined and the patient\nchart crashes on render (TypeError: undefined is not iterable),\nintermittently failing distro e2e runs.\n\nPinning swr to 2.2.5 in both packages aligns them with the app shell.\nPart of a coordinated set of pins (canonical PR:\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app#757).","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":3}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019Lb9FVhdM3v7tGH148nVf2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
